# Environment variables
#
# `.env` holds real credentials and is NEVER committed. It was, once, with live
# Neon credentials in it -- those are in the public history and have to be
# rotated, not just removed. `.env.example` is the tracked file: it documents
# every setting with placeholders.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Databases
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Local heavy-file store (CAD, meshes, result fields, vector indexes)
media_data/

# Reference manuals ARE tracked, deliberately and temporarily, so the corpus
# syncs to the Windows test workstation with a plain `git pull` instead of a
# manual copy. That is ~270 MB of vendor PDFs in the history, and it cannot be
# undone by a later .gitignore -- removing them needs a history rewrite. Revisit
# before this repository is published or cloned widely.
#
# The built index is NOT tracked. It is derived from the PDFs, it is rewritten
# whole on every build, and committing it would grow the repository on each
# rebuild while guaranteeing a binary conflict between any two machines that
# both ran setup. `scripts/setup.sh` / `setup.ps1` builds it on the target
# machine, which is the intended flow.
data/bm25/index/

# Logs
*.log

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
